    "body": "## Problem\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (hybrid full sparse-MLA + SWA + indexer + compressor) fails to boot on **SM120** (RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell / RTX 6000D) with two distinct block-size failures, because SM120 falls into the untested `else 128` buckets of the sparse-MLA and indexer backends:\n\n| Config | Result |\n|---|---|\n| block 128 (vLLM's choice for SM120) | config passes → kernel init crashes: `Assertion error: block_kv == 32 or block_kv == 64` (flashinfer `csrc/apis/attention.hpp`) |\n| block 64, unpatched | config error: `No common block size for 64 (FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_DSV41: [128])` |\n| block 64, sparse backend patched | config error: `No common block size for 64 (DEEPSEEK_V41_INDEXER: [128])` |\n| block 64, both patched (this PR) | ✅ boots and serves |\n\n## Root cause\n\nflashinfer's SM120 sparse-MLA/SWA kernels accept only 64-token pages — the same layout as the Hopper family (flashinfer#4380). 128-page is only valid on SM100, which runs the TRTLLM-gen/FlashMLA path. Both backends hard-code the 128 assumption for everything that isn't Hopper, so upstream effectively never booted DSV4.1 on SM120.\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo one-line conditional updates (SM100/Hopper behavior unchanged):\n\n1. `flashinfer_sparse.py` — the DSV41 sparse backend's `get_supported_kernel_block_sizes` now returns `[64]` on SM120\n2. `indexer.py` — `DeepseekV41IndexerBackend.get_supported_kernel_block_sizes` now treats SM120 like Hopper (64-page). The arch-12 fp4/fp8 indexer kernels support this layout; validated with `indexer_kv_dtype=mxfp4`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Boots and serves on 8x RTX 6000D (TP8 + EP, DSpark speculative decoding, 1M context) in continuous production across multiple nodes\n- Full acceptance suites pass (multi-tool agent traces, 128K–1M needle/math ladders, streaming-drop, fuzzed protocol cases)\n- SM100 paths untouched: the conditional only adds SM120 to the 64-page branch\n",
